in A Song of Ice and Fire and Game of  Thrones  dragonglass or obsidian is a mysterious  material with special magical properties  relating to White Walkers and dragons  it's used by the children of the forest  and the Nights Watch and may play an  important role in the ending of this  series so let's have a look  obsidian exists in the real world it's a  volcanic glass that forms from cold lava  historically obsidians been highly  valued because as well as being quite  beautiful it can be fractured to form  really sharp edges so for thousands of  years all over the world it's been used  to make tools and weapons like blades  and arrowheads as well as objects of  artistic and religious significance on  Easter Island the moai statues had  obsidian four eyes in anatolia mirrors  were made out of obsidian and in  mesoamerica the aztecs used obsidian  knives in bloodletting rituals and human  sacrifice now obsidian is used to make  surgical scalpels with blades sharper  than steel is considered a magical stone  by various new agey folks and is a high  tier crafting material in Minecraft and  Terraria so in a way we still seem to  value obsidian to this day anyway in  Game of Thrones obsidian has basically  the same physical properties that it has  in the real world it's apparently formed  from volcanic activity though there are  alternative theories its slick and shiny  and usually black though it can be other  colors it's very brittle and can form  razor-sharp edges and it's being used by  ancient peoples for thousands of years  though in Game of Thrones those people  aren't humans the original inhabitants  of Westeros are the Giants and the  children of the forest the Giants  apparently knew of no better tools or  weapons and branches pulled from trees  but the children of the forest had great  art in working obsidian and used it to  make tools and weapons for hunting  eventually human settlers came to  Westeros the first men and later the  Andals who all but wiped out the Giants  and children who now only survived in  small numbers north of the wall but the  humans value obsidian - its traded and  used in ornamentation in sword hilts and  rings and things crow food amber wears a  chunk of dragon glass in his empty eye  socket  so obsidian is around in small amounts  but it's only during the events of A  Song of Ice and Fire that people start  to realize just how important obsidian  is in clash Jon Snow finds a cache of  obsidian weapons wrapped up in a Night's  Watch cloak and buried on the fist of  the first men the cloak hasn't rotted  suggesting that the obsidian was  recently buried so it might have been  Benjen Stark who left it or maybe cold  hands for Bloodraven in the show it's a  bit different gran and Sam find the  cache beneath the stone marked with  ruins of the first man suggesting that  it might have been left by ancient  nights Watchmen whoever buried it Jon  takes some of the obsidian and gives it  to his friends in the watch Sam gets one  of the daggers and discovers its  importance when the others come the  others or White Walkers are strange icy  creatures from beyond the wall have been  killing humans and raising them as  whites basically zombies in an army of  the Dead  apparently intent on killing everything  that lives it may actually be more  complicated than that but either way  it's looking like the Nights Watch will  have to stop them  the whites can be killed with fire or by  chopping them into bits but the others  are really hard to kill they're  apparently invulnerable to most normal  blades and we've never seen them hurt by  fire the only thing to have seen kill a  white Walker at least in the books is  Sam's obsidian dagger when Sam stabs a  walker with obsidian the Walker  dissolves melts away its body smoking  and steaming where it touches the dagger  this stuff is like white Walker  kryptonite it has this fiery magic to it  which is hugely destructive to the icy  White Walkers  so the Nights Watch wants more obsidian  all they have now are the few daggers  and arrowheads and stuff that Jon took  from the fist of the first man and also  some wildlings of obsidian weapons  there's still lots more obsidian at the  fist or at hardhome in the show but with  all these whites and walkers around  it'll be too dangerous to go back for  the cash so as Jeor Mormont says they  need to find dragon class someplace else  luckily for the watch there are at least  four different places they could get  some firstly when Stannis Baratheon  comes to the wall he agrees with the  watch that they need to get more  obsidian to fight the others he says  that on the island of Dragonstone where  he originally ruled  there are tunnels full of obsidian whole  chunks of it boulders and ledges so  Stannis orders his men back on  Dragonstone to start mining this  obsidian the only problem is that in the  next book Dragonstone is besieged and  captured by the forces of King Tommen  and we don't know whether any of Stannis  is obsidian makes it off the island mace  Tyrell says that after its capture no  wealth is found on Dragonstone that  every inch of the island is searched and  not a single gemstone or speck of gold  is found though Kevan Lannister doubts  this so basically it's uncertain but  possible that some of the Obsidian mined  on Dragonstone makes it off the island  and is shipped towards the wall maybe to  arrive in the next book the second way  the watch could get obsidian is from  scar goes scar goes is a big island just  east of the wall and its people the scar  go see are infamous for savagery  cannibalism human sacrifice and  apparently riding unicorns in dance  devil set sail for Skoda's because  apparently Rickon stark is taken there  by OSHA so it looks like ska goes will  be an important location in the next  book and the thing is the skull GoSee  are known to offer obsidian blades in  trade ska goes may be an important  source of obsidian for the watch so with  any luck we'll soon see  Rickon stark riding a unicorn to the  wall with the big stash of dragonglass  to fight the others the third possible  source of obsidian is Valyria Valyria is  where the Targaryen xand that dragons  originally came from it was once the  center of a huge powerful Empire but was  destroyed in a massive mysterious fiery  apocalypse known as the doom of Valyria  we don't really know what caused the  doom but it seems to have been volcanic  and part of the destruction involved  dragonglass  raining down from the sky so presumably  there's still a whole lot of obsidian  lying around in the ruins of Valyria  Valyria is now considered a cursed  dangerous place avoided by just about  everyone but if say Daenerys Targaryen  was brave enough to stop off at our  ancestral homeland on our way to  Westeros she might just be able to pick  up a supply of obsidian imagine her  turning up at the wall when the walkers  come knocking bringing not only  fire-breathing dragons but enough  obsidian to arm every man on the  that would be a perfect way to stop the  others and for Daenerys to prove herself  to the realm she intends to rule this is  just speculation and George Martin has  been kind of ambivalent about whether  will actually see Valyria though it has  been shown in the show so we don't know  it seems maybe not likely but surely  possible that Dany will deliver obsidian  from Valyria the fourth possible source  of obsidian is the children of the  forest we know that they've used  obsidian for thousands of years we know  that the children still exist north of  the wall and we are told that the last  time the others came thousands of years  ago they were stopped with the help of  the children of the forest which seems  to have involved the children providing  the Nights Watch with obsidian this may  also be related to the legendary hero  azor Ahai or the last hero a figure who  apparently led humanity against the  white walkers with a flaming sword  called light bringer some fans  speculated that this magic sword may  have been made of obsidian or some  obsidian alloy because many of the  powers of light bringer can be explained  by the properties of obsidian it kills  white walkers it burns without being  consumed it can emit bright light a tale  of azor Ahai says when he stabbed a  monster with Lightbringer the creature  steamed and smoked and melted just like  a white Walker steams and smokes and  melts when Sam stabs it with obsidian so  there seems to be a connection here  between Azure ahyes magical sword and  obsidian maybe the children of the  forest will help us or a high Forge  another light bringer or maybe light  bringer was actually not one sword but  the many hundreds of obsidian weapons  given to the Nights Watch by the  children which over thousands of years  became the myth of a single hero with a  single magic sword  saving the world so now we don't know  the point here is that the children of  the forest may give the watch obsidian  and this could somehow be related to  this azor Ahai prophecy business and  that makes for really cool ways that the  Nights Watch could get obsidian to fight  the others and to decide the outcome of  what may be the biggest conflict in the  conclusion of the series but there's  still another reason why obsidian is  important glass candles glass candles  are magical artifacts from Valyria tall  twisted chunks of obsidian that can  function as candles they seem to be  closely connected to the power of  magic in the world apparently no one had  succeeded in lighting a glass candle for  many many years until the recent  reawakening of magic with the birth of  new dragons on the return of the White  Walkers in feast we see that Marlin the  mage has succeeded in lighting a glass  candle which symbolizes this magical  reawakening but glass candles aren't  just symbolic they're also very powerful  tools Mullen says that the sorcerers of  Illyria could see across mountain seas  and deserts with glass candles they  could enter a man's dreams and give him  visions and speak to one another half a  world apart we've actually already seen  this magic at work quaithe the  mysterious asha a shadow bender appears  to Daenerys in strange dreams and gives  her cryptic advice apparently using a  glass candle this use of fire magic to  see across long distances and enter  people's dreams contrasts with the magic  of the old gods and the weirwoods  which Bloodraven and brand news to do  the same things to see across long  distances and enter people's dreams the  way Melisandre and mokoro see visions in  their flames may also be related here  because it also seems a similar magic  using fire to see images so all this  gives a sense of order to the magic in  this world anyway we know Marwan and  Quaithe have glass candles and it's  actually possible that they're using  them to communicate and work together  because when Quaithe warns an heiress  about everyone who's coming for her she  leaves out Marwan as well as Quaithe and  Marwan glass candles are owned by the  other masters of the Citadel someone  called Ruth on night Walker in Qarth  and also the Targaryen szávay Mons day  seem to have had some we don't know much  about how these candles are being used  but they're obviously very powerful and  could play a big role in the future of  the series hopefully we'll learn more  about them while Sam is at the Citadel  anyway that is pretty much everything we  know about obsidian it kills White  Walkers  so the Nights Watch will probably need  some and luckily there are a bunch of  interesting ways they can get more there  are also glass candles which we don't  know much about but could also be really  important later on thanks for watching  feel free to like and subscribe if you'd  like to see more and thanks also to the  patrons who support this channel  including Travis cook Carson wilds  Caroline Faye on  monster mug chip Marshall snow and to  vine yard dog who requested this topic  special thanks also to Sean woods who  kindly allowed the use of his video  about making obsidian arrowheads there's  a link in the description if you'd like  to check out his channel so thank you  all again and comment below to let us  know what you'd like to see next  Cheers
 

